<rml>
<head>
	<title>Duel spectator frame (CDuelWatchMainFrameWindow)</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="duel_watch_frame.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="duel_watch_frame">
	<!-- The spectator's duel HUD (CDuelWatchMainFrameWindow), in the main HUD's place while the
	     duel-watch buff is on: the frame (menu_pk_01..03, 640 x 51) and the exit button always;
	     for a watched channel also the fighters' health and shield gauges (each with its catch-up
	     effect bar while it moves), their score marks (one per point, the count bound, the rows
	     laid out by the theme) and their names. Like the event HUDs, the workspace's
	     duel_watch_hud slot, in the footer beside the main HUD's, places #panel at the HUD's scale; the names take their native size
	     and cancel the scale. Only the exit button takes pointer events: its click is queued with
	     duel_watch_exit, C++ sends the channel quit request. -->
	<div class="screen">
		<div id="panel">
			<div id="back1"></div>
			<div id="back2"></div>
			<div id="back3"></div>
			<div id="fight" data-if="watching">
				<img class="gauge" data-for="g : gauges" data-attr-src="g.src" data-attr-rect="g.rect"
				     data-class-mirrored="g.mirrored" data-style-left="g.left + 'px'" data-style-top="g.top + 'px'"
				     data-style-width="g.width + 'px'" data-style-height="g.height + 'px'"/>
				<!-- A mark per point, each fighter's row stepping away from its own end of the frame. -->
				<div class="score-row" id="score_hero"><div class="score" data-for="hero_marks"></div></div>
				<div class="score-row" id="score_enemy"><div class="score" data-for="enemy_marks"></div></div>
				<span class="name counter-scaled" id="name_hero" data-style-font-size="hero_name.text_px + 'px'">{{hero_name.text}}</span>
				<span class="name counter-scaled" id="name_enemy" data-style-font-size="enemy_name.text_px + 'px'">{{enemy_name.text}}</span>
			</div>
			<div id="exit" data-event-click="duel_watch_exit" data-attr-data-hint="exit_hint"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
